## Configure inspector nib — derived from a stock OPENSTEP resource

`OpenStepMGAReplacementDisplay/English.lproj/DisplayInspector.nib` is built
by `OpenStepMGAReplacementDisplay/nib-src/build-inspector-nib.py` from
Configure.app's own display-inspector nib rather than authored from nothing.
It is stated here so the derivation is on the record rather than implied by
silence.  No Configure.app code is copied into this project; the nib is a
resource, and only the resource is derived.

## Mesa 3.4.2 — not in this repository, but in one of its packages

The accelerated `libGL_mga.a` is a COMPLETE alternative `libGL` built by
copying the OPENSTEP Mesa port's stock archive, replacing its `osmesa.o`
with one compiled with this project's hook point enabled, and adding this
project's back end.  It therefore contains Mesa code, and the
`OpenStepMGAMesaAccel` package carries Mesa's own `COPYRIGHT` and `COPYING`
byte for byte, including Mesa's statement that it is not a licensed OpenGL
implementation.  See `release-packaging/LICENSE_INVENTORY.md`.

The Mesa port itself is a separate project and this one does not modify it:
the package adds a second library beside the stock one rather than replacing
it (`docs/P1_PACKAGING_PRINCIPLE.md`).

